@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] profile-ai-rows-are-pullys
For a signed-in account the Profile sheet MUST list, under the account card, an AI search
group and a Providers group as Pully's Settings does. The Model row MUST show the chosen
model's name and its engine's own mark in colour, never a model ID or a robot icon. An
Effort row of its own MUST follow Model whenever the chosen model has more than one
effort, and the model page MUST NOT carry the efforts. Providers MUST list Claude Code and
Codex with their marks and whether each is signed in. The rows carry no lines that
explain them. Model, Effort and each provider open child pages inside the same Profile
sheet (`ui/menu/CONTRACTS` `card-sheet-pages-stay-in-the-sheet`). The rows MUST use
ThyMind's own sheet rows, type and colours, not Pully's look.
Source: Tavi, 28 October 2026 ("fully copy from the Pully project how it does sign-in for
those, how it puts them in the settings, its model and effort selectors"); pulls.review
`settings-model-row-names-the-model`, `settings-effort-under-model` and
`settings-no-helper-lines` at c71ee10d2f6fc1b279c5396076cfed5039f8dbd7.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] profile-ai-model-and-effort-pages
The model page MUST offer Claude Code and Codex as tabs, list the engine's recent models
first and the rest under Older models, mark the chosen one, and say so when the engine
is not signed in, linking to its sign-in page instead of a list. The effort page MUST
list the model's efforts by Pully's names, mark the model's default as Recommended and
end with Pully's footnote on what higher effort costs. Each engine MUST keep the model
last chosen for it on the phone, and changing the model MUST keep the chosen effort only
when the new model lists it.
Source: Tavi, 28 October 2026 (as `profile-ai-rows-are-pullys`); pulls.review
`ui/review/ModelPicker.kt` and `AiSettingsLogic` (ai-kit) at
c71ee10d2f6fc1b279c5396076cfed5039f8dbd7.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] profile-ai-sign-in-is-the-accounts
Claude Code and Codex MUST be signed in through the CLIs' own subscription sign-in on
Pully's pages: Claude Code's page code is pasted back, or taken from the clipboard when
the app returns to the front; Codex shows a device code and finishes by itself once it is
approved. The sign-in belongs to the signed-in ThyMind account and lives on the server,
never on the phone. Everything a page holds belongs to the session that opened it: a new
session MUST clear it and drop remembered sign-ins and model lists, and while the app is
in the background a page MUST NOT send requests, open pages or read the clipboard. A
refused AI request MUST NOT answer 401, because the app signs its session out on a 401.
Source: Tavi, 28 October 2026 (as `profile-ai-rows-are-pullys`); ai-kit
`kit-subscription-sign-in-only`; pulls.review
`android-provider-signin-keeps-its-session-on-browser-return` at
c71ee10d2f6fc1b279c5396076cfed5039f8dbd7.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] profile-shows-the-google-photo
For an account signed in with Google, the account button in the gallery and the Profile
sheet's account card MUST show the account's Google photo, sharp at the button's and the
card's size. The photo, name and email kept for the session MUST show at once when the
app starts and when the sheet opens, and MUST stay while the app is offline or the
server is slow; the sheet MUST NOT blank them while it asks the server again. A session
MUST NOT show another session's photo, and the photo MUST be fetched by a loader that
never carries the library session.
Source: Tavi, 28 October 2026 ("we also aren't loading the user's profile picture
properly, which we should").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] profile-connected-agents
For a signed-in account the Profile sheet's Account group MUST offer Connected agents above
Sign out, opening a page inside the same sheet that lists each AI app signed in through
ThyMind's MCP server by the name it gave itself, with when it connected and was last
used. Remove MUST ask once more on the same row before it signs the app out, and the app
MUST leave the list at once. The page MUST list only this account's AI apps, never a
phone or browser session, and removing one MUST NOT sign out the phone.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026 ("Nice. Build it." on the MCP brief, step 3: list and
remove your own MCP tokens, Rust routes plus a Profile row in the app).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] profile-feedback-sends-with-the-senders-ai
The Profile sheet MUST list a Send feedback row under Providers that opens a page with a text field,
Send, and under Send the line "Uses your Claude or Codex plan. Your change ships to
everyone using ThyMind." The page MUST offer only engines the account has signed in; with
none it MUST say "Sign in to Claude Code or Codex first" and take the person back to Providers. It MUST keep
its own engine, model and effort apart from AI search (the model and effort pages are
titled Feedback model and Feedback effort, search's Search model and Search effort), so a
feedback pick MUST NOT change AI search and an AI search pick MUST NOT change feedback.
With no model chosen it MUST start at the engine's first recommended model at medium. A
refusal MUST show the server's sentence and MUST NOT sign the account out.
Source: design_draft.md decision 4 and decision 5 (Tavi, 5 Nov 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] feedback-one-notification-per-job
A feedback job MUST have one notification, on the feedback channel, with the job id as its
identity, updated in place as the job moves and alerting only the first time, using the
server's title and detail. It MUST end in a final state (shipped, merged_server,
merged_not_released, no_change or failed), after which the phone MUST stop asking about
the job. A shipped job MUST start the update check, and its tap MUST open the app on the
update screen. A denied notification permission MUST NOT crash or block the job.
Source: design_draft.md decision 2 (Tavi, 5 Nov 2026).
